Live module patch — apply to /srv/vigo/stacks/stockpile/modules/package-upgrade.vgo

Three changes after agent upgrade to ≥0.37.19:

1. apt-update gains report_settled: true (suppresses daily "Created" → drift fix).
2. reboot-if-needed onlyif rewritten so the file-flag path actually triggers.
3. pkgin-upgrade unless uses dry-run (-n) instead of running the upgrade twice.

Apply with:
  sudo $EDITOR /srv/vigo/stacks/stockpile/modules/package-upgrade.vgo
  vigocli config publish

----- diff (against the version dated Apr 29 05:58) -----

@@ apt-update @@
   - name: apt-update
     type: exec
     when: os_family('debian')
     command: apt-get update -qq
     onlyif: find /var/lib/apt/lists -maxdepth 0 -mmin +1440 2>/dev/null | grep -q . || ! test -d /var/lib/apt/lists
+    report_settled: true   # cache refresh — counts as Settled, doesn't trip drift detection

@@ pkgin-upgrade (NetBSD) @@
   - name: pkgin-upgrade
     type: exec
     when: os('netbsd')
     command: pkgin update && pkgin -y full-upgrade
-    unless: pkgin upgrade 2>/dev/null | grep -q 'nothing to do'
+    unless: pkgin -n upgrade 2>/dev/null | grep -q 'nothing to do'
     timeout_secs: 600
     notify: [reboot-if-needed]

@@ reboot-if-needed @@
   - name: reboot-if-needed
     type: exec
     when: changed
     command: shutdown -r +1 'Rebooting after package upgrade'
-    onlyif: test -f /var/run/reboot-required || needs-restarting -r 2>/dev/null; test $? -eq 1
+    onlyif: (test -f /var/run/reboot-required) || (needs-restarting -r 2>/dev/null; test $? -eq 1)

----- end diff -----

Why each change:

1. apt-update: today's onlyif fires once a day (24h cache age), the command runs
   (returns 0), the agent reports Action::Created. Drift detection sees one Changed
   run per day and after 5 consecutive days (DivergedThreshold = 5) the envoy
   classifies as Diverged. report_settled: true tells the agent "this command's
   success is maintenance, not a state change" — it reports Action::None, the
   row shows Settled, ChangedCount stays 0, drift detection stays clean.

2. reboot-if-needed: the `||` short-circuits when /var/run/reboot-required
   exists, leaving $?=0 from the test -f. Then `test $? -eq 1` exits 1, so the
   onlyif fails and reboot never runs. Parenthesising the two paths fixes it.

3. pkgin-upgrade: bare `pkgin upgrade` is the real upgrade command; using it
   in unless ran the upgrade twice (once as the check, then as the action).
   `-n` is dry-run.
